{"id":"e997ae88fddff0119709dda8af7e5ba94abe1123","axis":"silent","repo":"apache/solr","sha":"e997ae88fddff0119709dda8af7e5ba94abe1123","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"changelog/unreleased/SOLR-17731.yml","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@","+title: >-","+  Fix v2 alias detail and collection snapshot creation requests returning HTTP 405.","+  Alias listings now return the same per-alias structure as the detail view,","+  including a collections array and properties; the Admin UI supports this format.","+  Align snapshot responses and error handling with v2 conventions, and migrate","+  the snapshot CLI to these APIs. The CLI explains when a snapshot is already absent","+  and returns a nonzero exit status for other deletion errors.","+  Fix asynchronous collection snapshot creation while preserving v1 response formats.","+type: fixed","+authors:","+  - name: Eric Pugh","+links:","+  - name: SOLR-17731","+    url: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/SOLR-17731"],"additions":14,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"dev-docs/apis-v2-conventions.adoc","lines":["@@ -160,7 +160,7 @@ Don't settle for a bare `SolrJerseyResponse` if the underlying operation actuall"," "," When an API exposes both a \"list all\" endpoint and a \"get one by name\" endpoint for the same kind of resource, give each its own response type rather than reusing the list's shape for a single item:"," ","-* `List<Resource>Response` - the collection endpoint's response. Its data is a map or list keyed/indexed across every matching resource (e.g. `ListAliasesResponse.aliases: Map<String, String>`).","+* `List<Resource>Response` - the collection endpoint's response. Its data is a map or list keyed/indexed across every matching resource (e.g. `ListAliasesResponse.aliases: Map<String, GetAliasByNameResponse>`)."," * `Get<Resource>Response` (or `Get<Resource>ByNameResponse`) - the single-resource endpoint's response. Its data is a flat object describing just that one resource, with no collection wrapper (e.g. `GetAliasByNameResponse.collections`, `GetAliasByNameResponse.properties`)."," "," Don't have the single-resource endpoint return the list type filtered down to one entry (e.g. a `Map<String, ...>` with one key) - that forces callers to re-extract by name something they already specified in the request, and conveys no information once only one key is possible."],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"solr/api/src/java/org/apache/solr/client/api/endpoint/CollectionSnapshotApis.java","lines":["@@ -53,9 +53,10 @@ CreateCollectionSnapshotResponse createCollectionSnapshot(","         throws Exception;","   }"," ","-  @Path(\"/collections/{collName}/snapshots/{snapshotName}\")","+  @Path(\"/collections/{collName}/snapshots\")","   interface Delete {","     @DELETE","+    @Path(\"/{snapshotName}\")","     @Operation(","         summary = \"Delete an existing collection-snapshot by name.\",","         tags = {\"collection-snapshots\"})"],"additions":2,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"solr/api/src/java/org/apache/solr/client/api/endpoint/DeleteAliasApi.java","lines":["@@ -25,10 +25,11 @@"," import jakarta.ws.rs.QueryParam;"," import org.apache.solr.client.api.model.AsyncJerseyResponse;"," ","-@Path(\"/aliases/{aliasName}\")","+@Path(\"/aliases\")"," public interface DeleteAliasApi {"," ","   @DELETE","+  @Path(\"/{aliasName}\")","   @Operation(","       summary = \"Deletes an alias by its name\",","       tags = {\"aliases\"})"],"additions":2,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"solr/api/src/java/org/apache/solr/client/api/model/CollectionSnapshotMetadata.java","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@","+/*","+ * Licensed to the Apache Software Foundation (ASF) under one or more","+ * contributor license agreements.  See the NOTICE file distributed with","+ * this work for additional information regarding copyright ownership.","+ * The ASF licenses this file to You under the Apache License, Version 2.0","+ * (the \"License\"); you may not use this file except in 